<article class="env-lemma" id="04FB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04FB">Lemma <span data-tag="04FB">37.7.9</span>.</a> Let $h : Z \to X$ be a formally unramified morphism of schemes over $S$. Let $Z \subset Z'$ be the universal first order thickening of $Z$ over $X$ with structure morphism $h' : Z' \to X$. The canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c_{h'} : (h')^*\Omega _{X/S} \longrightarrow \Omega _{Z'/S}  \]
</div>
  <p> induces an isomorphism $h^*\Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{Z'/S} \otimes \mathcal{O}_ Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map $c_{h'}$ is the map defined in Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01UV" data-tag="01UV">29.33.8</a>. If $i : Z \to Z'$ is the given closed immersion, then $i^*c_{h'}$ is a map $h^*\Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{Z'/S} \otimes \mathcal{O}_ Z$. Checking that it is an isomorphism reduces to the affine case by localization, see Lemma <a href="/tag/04FA" data-tag="04FA">37.7.8</a> and Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01US" data-tag="01US">29.33.3</a>. In this case the result is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04EF" data-tag="04EF">10.149.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>